  "title": "Rationalising the denominator",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "What rationalising means",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A surd on the bottom of a fraction is untidy. We make the bottom a whole number.",
          "write": "6/√3"
        },
        {
          "say": "That's called rationalising the denominator.",
          "write": "rationalise = rational bottom"
        },
        {
          "say": "Root b over root b equals 1. Multiplying by 1 doesn't change the value.",
          "write": "√b/√b = 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "And root b times root b is b, a whole number.",
          "write": "√b × √b = b"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
